  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of workers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Kiribati Trades Union Congress (KTUC) was established in 1982, representing workers in bank, port, maritime and overseas seamen, teachers, nurses, the public sector and general work. KTUC remains weak, losing memberships and with limited resources and influence in policymaking. In order to provide better services to its affiliates and reach out to new groups of workers, the KTUC wants to amend its constitution. It also intends to strengthen its leadership and office administrative functions through a series of training activities in the area of DWCP and SDGs, tripartism and social dialogue, leadership, FPRW including FoA and CB, membership drive, climate change and just transition, and minimum wages. ILO intervention aligns with KTUC&apos;s plan and expectations, which can eventually contribute to making KTUC stronger and more representative at the Decent Work Advisory Board (DWAB) and tripartite consultations, which will discuss and shape labour legislations and policies benefiting workers in all sectors.</narrative>
  </description>
